## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design runtime-extensible policy patterns using well-known design patterns and safe hot-swapping in production workloads.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for runtime behavior changes
- Registry/service-locator for dynamic strategy wiring
- Thread-safety and atomic swaps for hot-swapping
- Per-route configuration and isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
export interface IRateLimitStrategy {
  isAllowed(req: any, ctx: any): boolean;
}
export type StrategyFactory = () => IRateLimitStrategy;
export class StrategyRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, StrategyFactory>();
  register(name: string, factory: StrategyFactory) { this.map.set(name, factory); }
  resolve(name: string): IRateLimitStrategy {
    const f = this.map.get(name);
    return f ? f() : new (class implements IRateLimitStrategy {
      isAllowed() { return true; }
    })();
  }
}
