## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with runtime extensibility, decoupling, and error containment in a common frontend pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Publish/Subscribe
- Runtime extensibility
- Error isolation
- Minimal interfaces and registry

## Code Example
```javascript
interface Subscriber { onEvent(event: string, payload: any): void }
class EventBus {
  private map = new Map<string, Set<Subscriber>>()
  register(eventType: string, s: Subscriber) { this.map.get(eventType)?.add(s) }
  unregister(eventType: string, s: Subscriber) { this.map.get(eventType)?.delete(s) }
  publish(eventType: string, payload: any) {
    for (const s of this.map.get(eventType) || []) {
      try { s.onEvent(eventType, payload) } catch (e) { /* log and continue */ }
    }
  }
}
```

